Title:  I'm a record fan

Seq:    5.7.1.1.3

Level:  6 - Subdetail

Class:  quote

Attribution: [[Beatles, The|The Beatles]], 2000, from the book *[[The Beatles Anthology]]*


Body:

I was always slightly disappointed with all the performers I saw, from Little Richard to Jerry Lee. They never sound exactly like their records. I like “Whole Lotta Shakin’,” the 1956 take on the record, but I’m not interested in a variation on the theme. When Gene Vincent did “Be Bop A Lula” in Hamburg, he didn’t do it the same. It was a thrill to meet Gene Vincent and see him, but it was not “Be Bop A Lula.” I’m a record fan. — John Lennon
